			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 14 submodules for documentation standardization and webview stability\n\nPerform a mass update of all core Land Editor submodules to align documentation and runtime behavior. Most components (Air, Common, Echo, Grove, Mist, Mountain, Rest, SideCar, Sky, Vine, Wind, Worker) refine `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` with section emojis, bulleted lists, and absolute GitHub URLs for cross-referencing.\n\n**Cocoon**: Patch `Webview/Implementation.ts` to append a wildcard `font-src *` fallback to the Content Security Policy, resolving font loading failures in WKWebView where legacy protocol schemes are rejected.\n\n**Output**: Extend the `Logging` transform plugin to force injection of the `_vscodeApiScript` regardless of the `allowScripts` flag and ensure the CSP includes the font wildcard. This restores functionality for extensions like Roo Code and fixes custom font rendering.\n\n**Sky**: Refactor `Bridge.ts` to use bracket notation for dynamic `Wire` DTO property access, enforcing strict TypeScript compliance.\n\nThese updates ensure consistent technical documentation across the ecosystem and resolve critical webview rendering and API initialization issues on macOS.",
			"SHA": "c026dc1f1887ac086314e85b208affe799427d4b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T22:33:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⡟⠀⠀",
				26,
				14
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 13 core submodules for comprehensive architectural documentation\n\nPerform a mass synchronization of 13 key Land Editor submodules to introduce standardized `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` files and Mermaid visualizations across the entire backend and frontend ecosystem.\n\n**Air, Common, Echo, Grove, Mist, Mountain, Rest, SideCar, Sky, Vine, Wind, Worker**: Add detailed architectural overviews covering module responsibilities, design patterns (e.g., ActionEffect, work-stealing, effect-based services), and protocol definitions. Include Mermaid diagrams to visualize data flow, component interactions, and startup sequences for each domain.\n\n**Cocoon, Output**: Update with architecture documentation (Cocoon) and enhanced build pipeline diagrams (Output) alongside operational build artifact regeneration.\n\n**Sky**: Normalize string quote syntax in `Bridge.ts` and standardize dialog formatting in `window.confirm`/`window.prompt` calls to align with project style guidelines.\n\nThis synchronization establishes a unified technical reference for the editor's multi-process architecture, clarifying the separation of concerns between the Rust backend, TypeScript services, and UI layers.\n\nRefs: #CEL-ARCH-DOC-INIT",
			"SHA": "d2dc1761b4bd1bd960f9debaacdb74e35fd48d57"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:37:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output,Sky): Expose bridge metadata and enable cross-frame diagnostics\n\nEnhance observability for the UI bridging pipeline between the Sky component layer and the extension host by synchronizing updates in the Output build pipeline and Sky runtime.\n\n**Sky**: Refactor `_InstallSkyBridgeOnce` in `Bridge.ts` to expose execution metadata via `globalThis`. Introduce `__CEL_LAST_SET_HTML_INFO__` and `__CEL_LATEST_SET_HTML_INFO__` to capture view state and timestamps for `set-html` operations, enabling external debug inspection. Also standardize line breaks in `window.confirm` and `window.prompt` strings for consistent dialog formatting.\n\n**Output**: Extend the `RuntimeDiagnostics` transform plugin to leverage the new global metadata. Inject listeners for cross-frame `postMessage` traffic (capped at 50 events) and scheduled checks for the Sky bridge globals to report `SKY_SET_HTML` and `SKY_FIRST_SET_HTML` lifecycle events.\n\nThese changes provide granular telemetry for debugging UI communication and state synchronization issues within extension webviews.",
			"SHA": "7c04c5a988582342feab56f93c1518c29699b4e3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:36:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add runtime DOM state and React hook diagnostics\n\nInject comprehensive runtime diagnostics into the webview content pipeline to aid debugging of rendering issues and API availability in custom environments. The injected script now performs periodic DOM state checks (every 500ms) to monitor the presence and children of the root element, logs React internal hook status (renderer count), captures a full DOM snapshot at 5s, verifies `acquireVsCodeApi` availability, and dumps the initial body structure.\n\nThese diagnostics are scoped to the first 30 seconds of the session and provide detailed telemetry on the webview's lifecycle, ensuring robust observability for the `RuntimeDiagnosticsInner` transform plugin.",
			"SHA": "29862a1a65388c4d7de533be200d9c677685731d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:34:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Standardize escaped quotes in webview logging diagnostics\n\nCorrect the escaping of quote characters within the injected `DEBUG_WV` logging call in `Source/Plugin/Transform/Inject/Webview/Debug/Logging.ts`. Replace double-escaped quotes (`\\\"`) with single-escaped quotes (`\"`) for the `id=\"root\"` and `type=\"module\"` string checks.\n\nThis ensures the generated JavaScript string literals are syntactically correct and the runtime diagnostics correctly identify the presence of the React root element and module scripts during webview content processing.",
			"SHA": "436dcbfaf9fe2f806c2580039a0b7e0ea028b180"
